    "content": "The Ministry of Transport and Civil Aviation of Galmudug State has ordered a temporary suspension of all civilian flights operating from airports within the region. According to an official letter from Minister Cabdiqor Maxamed Maxamed, the directive takes effect on July 30, 2026, and remains in place for the duration of the ongoing elections or until further official notice from the ministry.\n\nThis measure is aimed at maintaining security and facilitating the orderly conduct of the electoral process. The decision comes as Galmudug prepares for key elections, during which authorities seek to prevent disruptions and ensure public safety.\n\nThe suspension affects both domestic and international civilian flights. Travelers are advised to check with airlines for rescheduling or alternative arrangements. The ministry has not specified whether cargo or humanitarian flights will be exempted.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this suspension may disrupt travel plans to and from Galmudug, particularly for those planning to participate in or observe the elections. Family visits and business trips could also be affected during this period.\n\nLocal stakeholders have called for clarity on the duration and scope of the ban. The ministry has indicated that flights will resume once the electoral process concludes or upon a revised directive.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/07/29/galmudug-oo-hakisay-duulimaadyada-rayidka-inta-lagu-jiro-doorashooyinka/",
