    "summary": "Galmodug's Electoral Commission has released voter registration results across 11 districts, with Gaalkacyo recording the highest number of registered voters at 65,950 ahead of upcoming elections.",
    "content": "The Independent Electoral and Boundaries Commission for Galmudug state has published the final tally of voter registration across all 11 districts in the region. According to the official data, Gaalkacyo district registered 65,950 voters, the highest figure among all districts. This marks a significant milestone for a city that serves as a key administrative and economic hub in the region.\n\nFollowing Gaalkacyo are Caabudwaaq with 48,358 registered voters and Hobyo in third place with a sizable number. The registration process was conducted over several weeks, with Commission teams operating in each district to ensure broad coverage. Local officials described the turnout as encouraging, particularly among women and youth.\n\nThis registration drive is part of preparations for Galmudug's upcoming parliamentary and presidential elections, which will determine the region's leadership for the next term. The Commission has emphasized that the process was independent and included verification measures to avoid double registration.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, these elections in Galmudug are a gauge of political stability and governance quality in the region. Many diaspora families originate from these districts, and the integrity and transparency of the electoral process can influence perceptions of security and investment opportunities back home. A well-conducted election could also boost confidence in returning or supporting development projects.\n\nThe next steps include candidate nomination and campaign periods, with election dates to be announced soon. The Commission has urged all registered voters to participate actively.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/07/29/gaalkacyo-oo-hoggaaminaysa-diiwaangelinta-codbixiyeyaasha-galmudug/",
