    "summary": "The National Independent Electoral and Boundaries Commission (NIEBC) has announced the total number of candidates running for the Galmudug State House of Representatives and Local Council elections. The data shows competition among 12 political parties for available seats.",
    "content": "The National Independent Electoral and Boundaries Commission (NIEBC) has officially disclosed the total number of candidates contesting in the upcoming elections for the House of Representatives and Local Council of the Galmudug State. According to the confirmed data released by the commission, the elections will feature a competitive field from various political organizations, with reports showing the allocation of seats for male and female candidates across different constituencies.\n\nCandidates from 12 political parties will be vying for positions in the Galmudug House of Representatives. The specific seat numbers and gender distribution have been published as part of the transparency measures. The commission's move to publicize these figures is aimed at keeping the public informed about the electoral process.\n\nThe elections in Galmudug are part of Somalia's broader political transition toward universal suffrage. Previous clan-based power-sharing models have slowly given way to party-led elections, although challenges remain in security and logistics. The upcoming vote is seen as a key test of the region's electoral readiness.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, particularly those from Galmudug, these developments offer insight into the political engagement back home. Diaspora members often participate through virtual outreach to candidates and parties, as direct voting from abroad remains limited. The transparency in candidate announcements could help inform their support and advocacy.\n\nThe NIEBC has urged parties to abide by electoral laws and maintain peaceful campaigning. Security preparations are underway across Galmudug to ensure safe voting, though concerns about potential disruptions persist.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/07/29/guddiga-doorashooyinka-oo-shaaciyay-tirada-musharaxiinta-golaha-wakiillada-iyo-deegaanka-ee-galmudug/",
